1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,885
Yesterday, I walked to the hills, and I saw three sheep!

2
00:00:06,285 --> 00:00:11,087
I didn't see the moon... but I saw a beautiful sunset.

3
00:00:11,537 --> 00:00:17,768
Walked. Saw. Didn't see. Mia is telling us about yesterday, and she is using the past simple.

4
00:00:18,368 --> 00:00:25,442
By the end of this lesson, you will be able to tell any story about the past, clearly and correctly. Let's start.

5
00:00:26,392 --> 00:00:31,499
We use the past simple for actions that started and finished in the past.

6
00:00:32,099 --> 00:00:38,587
The action is finished, and the time is finished too. Yesterday is finished. Last week is finished.

7
00:00:39,187 --> 00:00:49,249
Often we say the time: yesterday, last summer, in twenty twenty. And sometimes we don't say it, because the listener already knows it from the story.

8
00:00:50,199 --> 00:01:00,214
Here is the good news. The past simple is the same for every person. I walked, you walked, she walked, they walked. No extra s, no changes.

9
00:01:00,814 --> 00:01:05,089
For most verbs, we just add e d. Walk becomes walked.

10
00:01:05,689 --> 00:01:07,155
Play becomes played.

11
00:01:07,755 --> 00:01:09,348
Watch becomes watched.

12
00:01:09,948 --> 00:01:11,777
Visit becomes visited.

13
00:01:12,377 --> 00:01:16,237
Remember: the same form for I, you, he, she, it, we and they.

14
00:01:17,188 --> 00:01:21,561
Now, spelling. Most verbs simply take e d: walk, walked.

15
00:01:22,161 --> 00:01:26,275
If the verb ends in e, add only d: live, lived.

16
00:01:26,875 --> 00:01:33,275
If the verb ends in a consonant and y, change the y to i e d: study, studied.

17
00:01:33,875 --> 00:01:38,703
But if there is a vowel before the y, just add e d: play, played.

18
00:01:39,303 --> 00:01:46,898
And for short verbs that end consonant, vowel, consonant, double the last letter: stop, stopped. Plan, planned.

19
00:01:47,848 --> 00:01:51,607
The e d ending has three different sounds. Listen.

20
00:01:52,207 --> 00:01:58,719
After sounds like p, k, s, sh and ch, we say t: walked, watched, stopped, kissed.

21
00:01:59,319 --> 00:02:04,432
After voiced sounds and vowels, we say d: played, lived, cleaned, opened.

22
00:02:05,032 --> 00:02:11,645
And only after t or d, we add a new syllable, id: wanted, visited, needed, started.

23
00:02:12,245 --> 00:02:16,255
So we never say walk-ed. We say walked. One syllable.

24
00:02:17,355 --> 00:02:26,680
Let's watch Mia's evening again. Yesterday evening, Mia walked through the grass. She stopped near the sheep, and she counted them: one, two, three.

25
00:02:27,630 --> 00:02:32,825
Many common verbs are irregular. They don't take e d. You need to learn them.

26
00:02:33,425 --> 00:02:35,690
Go, went. I went to the hills.

27
00:02:36,290 --> 00:02:38,443
See, saw. She saw three sheep.

28
00:02:39,043 --> 00:02:40,925
Have, had. We had dinner.

29
00:02:41,525 --> 00:02:43,638
Eat, ate. He ate an apple.

30
00:02:44,238 --> 00:02:46,571
Come, came. They came home late.

31
00:02:47,171 --> 00:02:49,345
Take, took. I took a photo.

32
00:02:49,945 --> 00:02:52,325
Make, made. Grandma made soup.

33
00:02:52,925 --> 00:02:54,999
Buy, bought. Dad bought a map.

34
00:02:55,599 --> 00:03:02,962
Here's a tip: learn them in small groups of five, and say each one in a real sentence about your own day.

35
00:03:03,912 --> 00:03:09,924
Before negatives, one special verb: be. In the past, be has two forms: was and were.

36
00:03:10,524 --> 00:03:14,540
I, he, she and it take was. I was happy. It was cold.

37
00:03:15,140 --> 00:03:17,953
You, we and they take were. We were at home.

38
00:03:18,553 --> 00:03:23,794
The negative is wasn't or weren't. She wasn't tired. We don't use didn't with be.

39
00:03:24,394 --> 00:03:28,014
And questions start with was or were. Were you in the park?

40
00:03:28,964 --> 00:03:32,886
To make a negative, we use didn't, and then the base verb.

41
00:03:33,486 --> 00:03:34,968
I didn't see the moon.

42
00:03:35,568 --> 00:03:37,220
She didn't walk to school.

43
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:39,472
We didn't eat breakfast.

44
00:03:40,072 --> 00:03:41,525
They didn't go home.

45
00:03:42,125 --> 00:03:50,781
Very important: didn't already shows the past. So the main verb goes back to its base form. We say didn't go, never didn't went.

46
00:03:51,681 --> 00:03:56,483
I didn't see the moon... but I saw a beautiful sunset.

47
00:03:56,933 --> 00:04:01,965
For questions, put did before the subject, and again, use the base verb.

48
00:04:02,565 --> 00:04:06,468
Did you see the sunset? Yes, I did. Or: no, I didn't.

49
00:04:07,068 --> 00:04:09,556
Did Mia walk home? Yes, she did.

50
00:04:10,156 --> 00:04:15,717
With question words, did comes after them. Where did she go? She went to the hills.

51
00:04:16,317 --> 00:04:18,372
What did you eat? I ate soup.

52
00:04:19,272 --> 00:04:22,311
Did you see the sunset yesterday?

53
00:04:22,761 --> 00:04:27,609
These words tell us the time is finished, so they love the past simple.

54
00:04:28,209 --> 00:04:31,654
Yesterday. Last night. Last week. Last summer.

55
00:04:32,254 --> 00:04:36,922
Two days ago. A year ago. Ago always comes after the time.

56
00:04:37,522 --> 00:04:40,417
In twenty twenty. When I was a child.

57
00:04:41,017 --> 00:04:44,759
And this morning, but only when the morning is already finished.

58
00:04:45,709 --> 00:04:48,176
Let's fix some very common mistakes.

59
00:04:48,776 --> 00:04:53,913
He didn't went home. No. After didn't, use the base verb: he didn't go home.

60
00:04:54,513 --> 00:04:58,148
Did you saw the sunset? No. Did you see the sunset?

61
00:04:58,748 --> 00:05:07,148
I was go to school yesterday. In Arabic we can think was plus a verb, but in English we just say: I went to school yesterday.

62
00:05:07,748 --> 00:05:11,229
She goed to the park. Go is irregular: she went.

63
00:05:11,829 --> 00:05:18,276
I visit my grandma last week. Last week is finished, so: I visited my grandma last week.

64
00:05:19,226 --> 00:05:24,819
Now, let's practise your speaking. Listen, and repeat after me. Say it out loud!

65
00:05:25,719 --> 00:05:27,301
I walked to the hills.

66
00:05:30,301 --> 00:05:31,788
She saw three sheep.

67
00:05:34,788 --> 00:05:36,265
We didn't see the moon.

68
00:05:39,465 --> 00:05:40,889
Did you have dinner?

69
00:05:43,889 --> 00:05:45,367
They were very happy.

70
00:05:48,417 --> 00:05:55,000
Now, let's hear the whole story of Mia's evening. Listen, and notice every past simple verb.

71
00:05:56,100 --> 00:06:03,490
Yesterday evening, Mia walked through the soft grass. She saw some sheep near the old wall, and she stopped to count them.

72
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:10,096
Then I walked home, and I had dinner with Grandma.

73
00:06:10,696 --> 00:06:15,733
The sun went down. Mia didn't stay in the field. She walked home before dark.

74
00:06:17,046 --> 00:06:22,743
Now it's your turn. Choose the correct answer. You have five seconds for each question.

75
00:06:23,693 --> 00:06:26,995
Number 1. Yesterday I blank to the market.

76
00:06:32,795 --> 00:06:35,388
Went. Go is irregular: go, went.

77
00:06:36,288 --> 00:06:38,817
Number 2. She didn't blank the film.

78
00:06:44,617 --> 00:06:47,641
Watch. After didn't, we use the base verb.

79
00:06:48,541 --> 00:06:51,393
Number 3. blank you see Mia last night?

80
00:06:57,193 --> 00:06:59,405
Did. Did you see Mia last night?

81
00:07:00,305 --> 00:07:04,463
Number 4. We blank in London in 2020.

82
00:07:10,263 --> 00:07:13,757
Lived. The verb ends in e, so we add only d.

83
00:07:14,657 --> 00:07:17,558
Number 5. Stopped ends with the sound...

84
00:07:23,358 --> 00:07:25,604
T. Stopped. One syllable.

85
00:07:26,504 --> 00:07:31,353
Let's remember. The past simple is for finished actions at a finished time.

86
00:07:31,953 --> 00:07:40,034
It's the same for every person. Regular verbs take e d, with a few spelling rules, and the ending has three sounds.

87
00:07:40,634 --> 00:07:47,337
Irregular verbs need to be learned. And in negatives and questions, we use did, with the base verb.

88
00:07:48,287 --> 00:07:55,341
Here is your homework. Write five sentences about what you did yesterday in the comments. I will read them.

89
00:07:55,941 --> 00:08:02,799
If this lesson helped you, subscribe, and I'll see you in the next lesson: the past continuous. Goodbye!

